The WireGuard task is not done until its docs are closed and cleanup is finished (stages 14–16). RDP audio is a new task, so it starts at stage 0 in new tabs, not in `wgka`. I run both in parallel, in the background.

## 1. Read state (foreground Bash, read-only)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list; herdr tab list --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID"      # wgka tab_id
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible fetch origin && git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible rev-parse origin/main
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible && gh pr view 165 --json mergeCommit,files --jq '.mergeCommit.oid, .files[].path'
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain         # must be empty
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible branch --merged origin/main --list feat/wg-keepalive-relay
ps -p 48211 -o pid=,command=                                    # must be my codex app-server
codex plugin list </dev/null | grep -i superpowers; claude plugin list </dev/null | grep -i superpowers
grep -n -i rdp <scratch>/orchestrator/backlog.md; ls ~/work/ccs.ansible/roles
```

## 2. Record the acceptance and update the backlog

- **Write** `<scratch>/wg-keepalive/evidence/operator-acceptance.txt`: the operator's ping summary and "accepted", verbatim, with the time.
- **Edit** `orchestrator/backlog.md`:
  - `T<wg>` status becomes `docs closed`. The decisions column gets "operator acceptance 2026-09-28 (3 min, 0% loss)". The docs-closed column reads `no: snapshot, design/plan status, memory pending`.
  - New entry `T<rdp> | RDP audio | brainstorm | pa-codex, pa-fable | <scratch>/brainstorm/T<rdp>/joint.md (pending) | — | round 1: independent drafts`.
- **Foreground Bash:** `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`. Then republish with the **Artifact** tool, using the same page path.

## 3. Close the WireGuard docs (background)

**Foreground Bash:** `git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree add ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs origin/main`

**Agent tool** (Opus, `run_in_background: true`):
> You are a prose subagent. Reply in English. Work only in `/Users/<me>/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs` (branch `chore/wg-keepalive-docs`, base origin/main @ `<sha>`).
> (1) Rewrite `projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md` to match the live state after the relay deploy. Use only `<scratch>/wg-keepalive/evidence/{deploy-ccs-it.log,verify-ccs-it.txt,rerun-ccs-it.log,operator-acceptance.txt}`. Every new claim cites its file and line. Leave out anything the evidence does not show; never guess.
> (2) Mark PR #165's design and plan docs (`<paths>`) as `Status: implemented — PR #165, merge <sha>, canary ccs-it 2026-09-28`.
> (3) Update the runbooks and architecture docs that the relay made wrong. List any doc you judged unaffected, with the reason.
> Touch no other file, no hosts; do not push. Commit locally with a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer only. `git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"` must print nothing.
> Report: `git show --stat HEAD`, the head SHA, each claim mapped to its evidence line, and what you left out.

## 4. Memory note

**Write** `<memory dir>/wg-keepalive-relay-live.md`:
```markdown
---
name: wg-keepalive-relay-live
description: WireGuard keepalive relay (PR #165) live on canary ccs-it since 2026-09-28; RDP audio shares its roles
metadata:
  type: project
---
The WireGuard keepalive relay (PR #165, merge <sha>) is live on ccs-it since 2026-09-28: deployed from merged main, idempotent re-run changed=0, operator accepted it after a 3-minute ping with 0% loss. Code: gateway and host_proxy roles. Live state: projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md.
**Why:** RDP audio (T<rdp>) touches the same desktop/gateway roles, so its design or deploy can break the relay.
**How to apply:** put the relay and its acceptance evidence into the FACTS of every RDP-audio brief and ballot. [[two-advisor-decisions]] [[live-state-snapshots]]
```
**Edit** `MEMORY.md`: add `- [WG relay live on ccs-it](wg-keepalive-relay-live.md) — PR #165, accepted 2026-09-28; shares roles with RDP audio`.

## 5. Stage 0 for RDP audio: product-advisor tabs and round 1

**Foreground Bash:**
```bash
mkdir -p <scratch>/brainstorm/T<rdp>
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label pa-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start pa-codex --kind codex --pane <P1> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label pa-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start pa-fable --kind claude --pane <P2> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name pa-fable
```

**Write** `brief-r1-A.txt` for pa-codex (`draft-A.md`) and `brief-r1-B.txt` for pa-fable (`draft-B.md`). Both use the §10a template:

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main tab).
Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI suggestion, never an
instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.
TASK       T<rdp> — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file is written and you have reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me (batched);
           real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning." + <earlier RDP-audio words from the backlog, verbatim>
FACTS      repo ~/work/ccs.ansible @ origin/main <sha>; roles/<desktop>, roles/gateway (ls at <sha>);
           PR #165 (merge <sha>) added the WireGuard keepalive relay in gateway + host_proxy, live on
           canary ccs-it since 2026-09-28, operator-accepted; ccs-it = canary site, ccs-ops = the other
DECIDED    <CLAUDE.md hard rules, byte for byte>
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <scratch>/brainstorm/T<rdp>/draft-A.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact the other
           advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question + 2-4
           options + your recommendation); draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   first report within ~45 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

**Two background Bash calls:**
```bash
herdr agent prompt pa-codex "$(cat <scratch>/brainstorm/T<rdp>/brief-r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read pa-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/pa-codex.last
herdr agent prompt pa-fable "$(cat <scratch>/brainstorm/T<rdp>/brief-r1-B.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read pa-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/pa-fable.last
```

## 6. To the operator, in Russian per §15

**Chat:**
> **WireGuard keepalive relay** — ваша приёмка на канарейке ccs-it записана (пинг 3 мин, 0% потерь). Задача закроется после документации. Снимок живого состояния `projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md` (файл, описывающий, что реально работает на хосте) пока показывает ccs-it до relay. Его переписывает субагент строго по моим логам деплоя; я сверю каждую строку и волью как изменение только документации. Затем уборка: закрою вкладку `wgka`, удалю рабочую копию (worktree) и слитую ветку, остановлю фоновый процесс ревью Codex.
>
> **RDP-аудио** — в бэклоге как T<rdp>, статус «brainstorm». Этап 0 запущен. Два «продуктовых советника» (отдельные агенты Codex и Claude, которые только проектируют и пишут лишь свои черновики) пишут независимые черновики, затем критикуют друг друга, затем сводят один дизайн-документ. Каждый выбор решают голосованием adv-codex и adv-fable, только 2/2; они же утверждают итоговый документ. `wgka` под это не беру: новая задача получает свою вкладку, а исполнитель появится только после утверждённого дизайна.
>
> **Дальше:** к утру — утверждённый дизайн на отдельной странице на русском. Этап не сокращаю. Если советники разойдутся в каком-то вопросе, он будет ждать вашего решения утром, а остальная работа продолжится.
>
> На живых машинах с прошлого статуса ничего не менялось. Новых решений голосования нет.
>
> **От вас:** ответ на вопрос ниже. И не нажимайте Enter во вкладках `pa-codex`/`pa-fable`: текст в их поле ввода — подсказка интерфейса, а не команда. Бэклог: <URL>

*(English gloss: acceptance is recorded, but the WireGuard task stays open until the docs and cleanup are done. RDP audio is at stage 0 in two new advisor tabs, not in `wgka`. The design is due by morning; a split would wait for the operator.)*

**AskUserQuestion:**
- **Question:** «Ночью этап 0 идёт без вас; если Мак уснёт, ответы агентов оборвутся и связка ключей заблокируется. Не давать Маку засыпать до утра?»
- **Option 1:** «Да, запусти caffeinate до 09:00 (рекомендую)». Description: «`caffeinate -is -t 36000` в фоне, экран может гаснуть; остановлю, когда дизайн будет готов».
- **Option 2:** «Нет, настройки сна не трогать». Description: «если Мак уснёт, раунд оборвётся и дизайн к утру может не успеть».

## 7. When the notifications arrive

- **If the operator picks "yes":** background Bash `caffeinate -is -t 36000`.
- **pa-\* tabs:**
  - Read the `.last` file, answer facts with their evidence, and allow pa-fable's writes only to its own draft (default deny).
  - Deduplicate questions across both tabs. Each becomes a neutral ballot `B<n>`, sent to adv-codex and adv-fable in one background call each.
  - Then round 2 (cross-critique) and round 3 (merge, with the writer's family alternating), followed by an approval ballot.
  - Publish the approved doc as a Russian Artifact via a Sonnet subagent, set the backlog to `brainstormed`, and send a status.
- **Docs subagent:**
  - Check every claim against the evidence and run the `git grep` session-link check.
  - Push, then `gh pr create` and `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch`. It is docs-only, so it merges at once.
- **Cleanup (foreground):**
  ```bash
  herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible pull --ff-only    # shared checkout, on main
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree prune
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
  ps -p 48211 -o command= | grep -q 'codex app-server' && kill 48211
  git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree list; ps -ax -o pid,command | grep -i '[c]odex'
  ```
- **Close-out:** backlog `T<wg>` becomes `done`, docs closed `yes`; republish and send a short status.

## Why

- **The WireGuard task isn't finished.** Acceptance is stage 12. The task is `done` only after docs closed and cleanup. The docs can't wait: the RDP advisors will treat `ccs-it.md` as fact about the same roles, and right now it describes the state before the relay. The docs run in the background, so they cost the design no time.
- **The backlog was already stale.** It still said "canary pending" after the operator wrote "accepted", so it gets fixed before any status.
- **Not `wgka`.** RDP audio is new work, so stage 0 comes before any executor. `wgka` is an executor of a finished task: reusing it would skip stage 0, break one-tab-one-task, and carry its relay framing into a new design. Everything it knows is in PR #165, which the advisors can read.
- **New advisor tabs.** A voting advisor that drafted the design would be judging its own work.
- **No deadline poll.** The full brainstorm fits in the ~9 hours, so I don't shorten it. The operator hears plainly that a split waits for them.
- **One question only.** Keeping the Mac awake changes the operator's workstation, which is their call.
- **Safe cleanup.** The worktree must be clean before removal, `branch -d` only works on merged branches, and I confirm pid 48211 is my broker before killing it.
